WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.760
In this two-part
series on gray hair,

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.360
I will go through why hair turns grey,
what's the role of genetics,

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.234
and what we can do about it.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:17.084
"Why Does Hair Turn Gray?"

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.440
The graying of hair is one of
the most obvious signs of aging.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.720
It's also known by a technical
term that I had never heard of,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.160
"canities."

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.600
The first time I saw the word,
I misread it,

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.240
wondering what gray hair
had to do with dentistry.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.600
Evidently, gray hair
isn't really white,

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.440
but the pale yellowish tinge

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.160
of the constitutive
keratin protein,

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.640
but, like polar bears,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.600
it just looks white by the way
light reflects off of it.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.280
Why is hair pigmented
in the first place?

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.880
Some suggest it may be
for detoxification,

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.760
as natural toxins
like heavy metals

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.960
bind to the pigment melanin
to be excreted from the body

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.800
through hair outgrowth.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.720
That's why you can estimate
the amount of fish consumption

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.160
from the mercury content
of children's hair clippings,

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.720
why "[a]nalysis of hair mercury

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.000
may be warranted
before pregnancy"

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.080
in women who eat a lot of fish,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.880
and why the levels
of mercury in the hair

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.800
of those eating plant-based
diets were found to be

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.840
up to ten times lower than those
who just occasionally ate fish.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.360
Within three months of switching
to a plant-based diet,

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.120
the levels of mercury, lead, and
cadmium growing out in your hair

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.360
appear to drop significantly

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.680
but build back up
when meat and eggs

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.760
are added back into the diet.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.600
Enough with the science trivia.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.360
What causes our hair
to turn gray,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.400
and what can we do about it?

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.120
In medical school,
you learn about

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.160
the so-called 50-50-50 rule.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.880
By the age of 50,
the dictum goes,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.400
50 percent of the population

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.240
has at least 50 percent
gray hair.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.240
But that was based on
a homogenous population

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:04.440
of largely white,
fair-haired Australians.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.680
The global range is more like
6 percent to 23 percent

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.920
are 50 percent gray by 50.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.320
Though not as memorable
an axiom,

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:18.560
it looks like 75 percent or so
of people 45 to 65 years old

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.560
have about 25 percent gray hair.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.880
Those of African
or Asian descent

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.560
tend to show less gray hair.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.040
White people generally start
to gray in their mid-30s,

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.720
Asians in their late 30s,

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.360
and Africans in their mid-40s,

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.080
such that premature graying
is defined

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.400
before 20 in Caucasians

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.880
but before 30
in African Americans.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.520
Age 25 has been suggested
as a cutoff for India.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.000
Premature or not,

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.640
what causes hair to turn gray
in the first place?

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.000
The hair follicle is
a complex little mini-organ

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.040
that anchors and grows
a single hair.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.680
In the base of the follicle bulb

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.400
as few as 100
pigment-making cells

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.680
normally stain the emerging hair
shaft with melanin pigments

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.240
that can range in color
from black to red.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:17.560
A single hair grows for about
3.5 years before falling out

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.880
and a new one starts
growing in its place.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:24.960
So, graying may start
after about 10 hair cycles

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:30.000
when pigment deposition declines
as the pigment generating cells,

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.800
called melanocytes,
start to become depleted.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.720
What kills them off?

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:39.320
There's a depigmentation
disorder called vitiligo

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.640
where melanocytes
in the skin are killed off

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.600
by the buildup
of hydrogen peroxide,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.800
which can decompose
into toxic free radicals.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.760
So, researchers checked,
and indeed,

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:55.400
the same "massive" levels were
found in aging hair follicles.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.920
Where does the hydrogen peroxide
come from?

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.680
It's naturally generated as a
by-product of melanin synthesis,

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.400
but normally countered
by an antioxidant enzyme

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.040
called catalase.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.200
The problem, it seems,
is that catalase

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.160
and other antioxidant defenses
may decline as we age

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.400
and leave melanocytes vulnerable

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:21.360
to their own hot potato
production of pigment.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.200
Our own eyelashes present
"an enigma in plain sight."

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.040
Eyelashes tend to be the
darkest hairs on the human body

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.600
and undergo graying
significantly later

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.200
than other hairs.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.680
The explanation appears to be

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.080
the presence of a particular
antioxidant protein

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.080
missing from regular hair,

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.560
consistent with the prevailing

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:59.640
"free radical
theory of graying."

